# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings, regardless of core.autocrlf on any
# given machine — a CRLF shebang line (e.g. "#!/bin/bash\r") makes Linux look for an interpreter
# literally named "/bin/bash\r", which doesn't exist, failing with a misleading
# "exec ./script.sh: no such file or directory" even though the file is clearly present. This bit
# containerization/docker/fhirbridge-app/entrypoint.sh specifically: it's COPY'd into a Linux
# container image and run directly as ENTRYPOINT, so a Windows checkout with CRLF broke every build
# until this was added.
*.sh text eol=lf
